 TaggingRules->{"TemplateGroupName" -> "LongDescription"},
 DefaultNewCellStyle->"Text",
 CellTags->{"Basic Description", "LongDescription", "TemplateCellGroup"},
 CellID->97826971,ExpressionUUID->"90657ced-8d5e-407c-b374-6c0830d095d4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This repository contains experimental code and a developing language for \
geometry emerging as an effective description of large graphs at a large \
observer scale, aligned with the vision of ",
 ButtonBox["Stephen Wolfram",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://writings.stephenwolfram.com/"], None}],
 ". Our goal is to demonstrate how ",
 StyleBox["Euclidean, Riemannian, and symplectic geometry",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " emerge in limits of graphs. We view a graph as a webbing of paths and seek \
the essence of geometry in this webbing. An essential element is an observer \
who determines properties of the observed geometry. The eventual goal of \
infrageometry is to explain the emergence of space in hypergraph rewriting \
models of the universe, as described in the ",
 ButtonBox["Wolfram Physics Project technical introduction",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://www.wolframphysics.org/technical-introduction/"], None}],
 ". Note that hyperedges are not needed to recover the classical geometries."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3833257e-43f0-4e18-8e46-db6bc959c8f0"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "Details",
 Cell[BoxData[
  PaneSelectorBox[{True->
   TemplateBox[{"Details", 
     Cell[
      BoxData[
       FrameBox[
        Cell[
        "Details may include a long description of the resource's contents, \
history, methodology or other relevant information. Give references here if \
they are directly relevant to the resource. The details will appear above the \
examples on the webpage for the resource.", "MoreInfoText"], Background -> 
        GrayLevel[0.95], FrameMargins -> 20, FrameStyle -> GrayLevel[0.9], 
        RoundingRadius -> 5, ImageSize -> {
          Scaled[0.65], Automatic}]], "MoreInfoText", Deletable -> True, 
      CellTags -> {"SectionMoreInfoDetails"}, 
      CellMargins -> {{66, 66}, {15, 15}}]},
    "MoreInfoOpenerButtonTemplate"]}, Dynamic[
    CurrentValue[
     EvaluationNotebook[], {TaggingRules, "ResourceCreateNotebook"}]],
   ImageSize->Automatic]],ExpressionUUID->
  "123e0a93-f3f5-44ef-af0c-a2442d203202"]
}], "Subsection",
 Editable->False,
 Deletable->False,
 TaggingRules->{"TemplateGroupName" -> "Details"},
 DefaultNewCellStyle->"Notes",
 CellTags->{"Details", "TemplateCellGroup"},
 CellID->280804237,ExpressionUUID->"57b49300-26a8-40af-859e-be7b6e0631cf"],

Cell["\<\
Infrageometry asks which geometric objects and measurements can be defined \
intrinsically on a graph for a given observer, and when they converge to \
their classical counterparts along sequences of graphs. Dimension, curvature \
and symmetry are aggregated properties of the substrate that are measured \
rather than assumed.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"173dd1ee-6326-4425-9d62-91f9823277a2"],

Cell["\<\
Everything is computable at every level, so the framework is code. Where \
classical geometry prizes uniqueness and well-definedness, infrageometry \
enumerates every case, keeps the branching, aggregates robust observables and \
does statistics over them.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"88f0822d-ac0d-424b-83bd-9b382b825f26"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Install with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   ButtonBox["PacletInstall",
    BaseStyle->"Link"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
